<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<task id="059" project="spaarke-ontology-platform-r1">
  <metadata>
    <title>Worklist widget assembly: two lanes, count filters, narrative slot, aggregate row, disclosures</title>
    <phase>5 The worklist surface</phase>
    <gate>038, 051, 052, 054, 058 complete</gate>
    <status>not-started</status>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>Composes the Console's primary surface from the read route, the row, the filters and the wizard.</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>sonnet</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>Assembly of already-built pieces into one registered widget, behaviour fixed by HANDOFF section 1.2 and 1.4.</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>high</effort>
    <parallel-group>none</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>false</parallel-safe>
    <parallel-reason>055 deploys it and 064 swaps the Briefing tab to it.</parallel-reason>
    <deps>038, 051, 052, 054, 058</deps>
    <tags>frontend,fluent-ui,react,widget</tags>
    <estimated-effort>4-6 hours</estimated-effort>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>Assemble the worklist widget: read both lanes from the Signal read route, render one MatterCard per matter with IssueLines, per-lane count filters on the extended MetricCard, the narrative slot, the email aggregate row and the closed/suppressed disclosures, and open the decision wizard on the browse set the user is looking at.</prompt>
  <role>SPAARKE front-end developer. Membership and order come from the server; the widget never sorts or filters by its own rule.</role>
  <goal>A registered workspace widget renders Decide above Do from real data, its filters are honest, and every line opens the wizard on the visible list.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>Reconciliation W-1..W-12 and HANDOFF section 1.2 / 1.4 L115-124 (binding): two lanes, Decide always above Do; each lane has a heading with its count and a start button that walks the visible (filtered) list; count cards per lane; "Showing n of m - Show all"; "+1 other open item on this matter, not in this filter"; filters not remembered between sessions; the narrative summarises Do volume and is hidden while a filter is on; one aggregate email row at the top of the Do lane, not in either lane's counts; Closed today, Suppressed (with until-date) and Closed earlier behind disclosures. D-15: rows come only from the BFF read route (task 038). D-26: the wizard opens in-app.</background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="new">src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/components/Worklist/WorklistWidget.tsx</file>
      <file role="modify">src/client/shared/Spaarke.AI.Widgets/src/widgets/workspace/register-workspace-widgets.ts</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/solutions/LegalWorkspace/src/sections/dailyBriefing/dailyBriefing.registration.ts</file>
    </relevant-files>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="owner">Scope (D-15): the widget reads Signals ONLY through the task 038 route; no Xrm.WebApi or child-records read of sprk_signal anywhere in the widget.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Scope: order is the route's order; the widget never re-sorts. Filters are lenses on the lane's list (task 052), never another query, and are not persisted (no localStorage or user setting).</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Scope: the aggregate email row is task 054's AggregateCard at the top of the Do lane, its count taken from the same feed the Email Review tab uses (#36), excluded from both lanes' counts and hidden under a Do filter.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Scope: the narrative slot shows the existing Briefing narrative (task 062 makes it summarise Do volume) and is hidden while any filter is on; it may not name an item that is not on the list (#38).</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Scope: the widget lands in a shared library and is registered through WorkspaceWidgetRegistry; nothing but registration in src/solutions/SpaarkeAi (FR-28).</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-021">Scope: Fluent v9 tokens only; light and dark correct; keyboard reachable.</constraint>
    <constraint source="owner">AMENDED 2026-10-07 (D-34, D-35): both lanes render one card per CORE record (matter or project); the reader's own items with no core record appear in their Do lane under a "Not filed" group (last in the lane, included in the Do counts). Filters and the "+1 other open item" line work per core record.</constraint>
    <constraint source="owner">AMENDED 2026-10-07 (D-36): one card per core record of ANY core type (matter, project, work assignment, service request), grouped by (sprk_corerecordtype, sprk_corerecordid); no per-type code.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">ADDED 2026-10-09 from task 051 (#1513): the host passes MatterCard `visibleList` (the lane's browse set, not one card's items) and `onOpenItem`; each item carries `pastDueWording` from 038's response ("late" for work assignments). See notes/051-worklist-row-component-notes.md.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
    <topic>Workspace widgets</topic>
    <files>
      <file>docs/guides/BUILD-A-NEW-WORKSPACE-WIDGET.md</file>
      <file>docs/architecture/SPAARKEAI-DASHBOARD-AND-WIDGET-MODEL.md</file>
      <file>docs/standards/ASSISTANT-UI-ELEMENT-CRITERIA.md</file>
      <file>projects/spaarke-ontology-platform-r1/notes/v4-reconciliation.md</file>
      <file>projects/spaarke-ontology-platform-r1/spec.md</file>
    </files>
    <patterns>
      <pattern name="Widget registration" location="src/solutions/LegalWorkspace/src/sections/dailyBriefing/dailyBriefing.registration.ts">The registration template.</pattern>
    </patterns>
  </knowledge>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="0" name="Context + rigor declaration">Declare the rigor level and reason per root CLAUDE.md section 8, then load the knowledge files above before touching code. Record the reconciliation section B.6 pre-start check (HANDOFF section 1.2 all, section 1.4 L115 and L121-124, section 1.1 L51-53) in task notes.</step>
    <step order="1">Build the widget against the 038 route contract with fixtures.</step>
    <step order="2">Wire lanes, filters, honesty lines, narrative slot, aggregate row and disclosures.</step>
    <step order="3">Open the wizard (058) on the visible list for a line, a lane's start button, and the disclosures.</step>
    <step order="4">Register the widget; tests per behaviour above.</step>
    <step order="5">Update tasks/TASK-INDEX.md: set this task to the completed marker, AND set this POML status element to completed. Both, or scripts/check-task-status-drift.ps1 fails the next push.</step>
    <step order="6">Record any deviation from this POML in projects/spaarke-ontology-platform-r1/notes/.</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>If a behaviour in HANDOFF section 1.2 needs data the 038 route does not return, STOP and extend the route through its own task rather than reading Dataverse from the widget.</trigger>
    <trigger>If grouping, filters or counts would need to name a specific core type (D-36 extensibility), STOP and escalate rather than adding a type branch.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <justification>
    <existing>The Daily Briefing widget (LegalWorkspace dailyBriefing section) is the current surface; it reads the collector, not Signals, and has no lanes, filters or wizard.</existing>
    <extension>No: the Briefing is replaced by this widget in task 064 (BR-4), and its sections are kept behind a flag for one release rather than mutated in place.</extension>
    <cost-of-doing-nothing>The row, filters and wizard exist with no surface composing them, so Signals stay invisible (the sprk_spendsignal outcome).</cost-of-doing-nothing>
  </justification>

  <ui-tests>
    <test name="Decide above Do with honest filters">
      <steps>
        <step>Seed several Do items and two Decide items; open the worklist; click one Do count card</step>
      </steps>
      <expected>Decide renders above Do; the Do list filters in place with "Showing n of m - Show all"; the narrative hides; the aggregate row hides.</expected>
    </test>
    <test name="Wizard opens on the visible list">
      <steps>
        <step>With a filter on, click a line, then use the wizard's next arrow to the end</step>
      </steps>
      <expected>The wizard browses only the filtered list and does not wrap.</expected>
    </test>
    <test name="Dark mode compliance per ADR-021">
      <steps>
        <step>Toggle dark mode and open every disclosure</step>
      </steps>
      <expected>All surfaces adapt via semantic tokens.</expected>
    </test>
  </ui-tests>

  <tools>
    <tool name="npm">Build and test the client packages</tool>
  </tools>

  <outputs>
    <output type="code">src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/components/Worklist</output>
    <output type="code">src/client/shared/Spaarke.AI.Widgets/src/widgets/workspace/register-workspace-widgets.ts</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">Given both lanes populated, when rendered, then Decide is above Do and each lane shows its count and start button.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given a filter, when on, then the lane shows "Showing n of m - Show all", a matter with an open item outside the filter shows the "+1 other open item" line, and the narrative and aggregate row are hidden.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given a reload, when the widget renders, then no filter is restored.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given the aggregate row, when counted, then it is excluded from both lanes' counts and its number equals the Email Review feed's count.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given the Closed today, Suppressed and Closed earlier disclosures, when opened, then each lists its set (Suppressed with the until-date) and opens the wizard read-only.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: the widget performs no direct sprk_signal read and never re-sorts the route's order.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Tests cover the behaviours above; anything beyond needs a one-line justification in task notes. The packages build.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given project-grouped items and Not filed items, when the worklist renders, then each project has its own card and the reader's Not filed items appear only in their Do lane under Not filed (D-34, D-35).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given items grouped under a work assignment and a service request, when the worklist renders, then each has its own card (D-36).</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>spec.md FR-24 (amended), FR-29, FR-34, FR-54; D-15, D-26. Reconciliation W-2, W-9..W-12.</notes>

  <execution><skill>.claude/skills/task-execute/SKILL.md</skill></execution>
</task>
